# Netlify security headers. Files in public/ are copied to the dist root, so
# Netlify picks this up automatically on deploy. Applies to every route.
#
# IMPORTANT: connect-src must list every origin the app talks to. It currently
# allows Supabase (auth + realtime) and a Render-hosted backend. If you move the
# backend off *.onrender.com, add its origin here or the browser will block the
# API calls (CSP failures show up as "Refused to connect" in the console).
#
# connect-src MUST also include `blob:` and `data:` — Results Hub Download/Share
# `fetch()` the before/after result images, which are blob:/data: object URLs the
# app minted. fetch() is policed by connect-src (unlike an <a href download>, which
# is navigation), so without these two schemes the download/share fetch is refused.
#
# worker-src 'self' blob: — browser-image-compression spawns a Web Worker from a
# blob URL; without an explicit worker-src it falls back to script-src 'self' and
# the worker is blocked (compression then silently runs on the main thread).
/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=()
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob:; font-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' blob: data: https://*.supabase.co wss://*.supabase.co https://*.onrender.com; worker-src 'self' blob:; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'
